From 78df613b8dc2a54dc05b5c9ec819f91a3c9f2027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:08:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: Titin's answers on icon, text and
 inactive colors

- Toolbar icons: #656666 light, #EDEEF1 dark.
- Tab text: black on light, white on dark for the active tab; inactive
  tabs use it at 50% over the tab strip, composited to an opaque color
  because Chromium's tab code expects opaque foregrounds. Regular windows
  only: private and Tor windows keep Brave's colors (Titin designs them
  separately).
- Window without focus: the frame is a little dimmer, with Chromium's
  recipe for the inactive header (ui/color/sys_color_mixer.cc) applied to
  Titin's frame colors.
- Bookmark folders: flat, in the toolbar icon color.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
